,\n      \"renderer\": \"cluster_size_barplot\",\n      \"filename\": \"cluster_size_barplot.png\",\n      \"title\": \"Cluster Size Summary\",\n      \"description\": \"Spot or cell counts for the primary Leiden clusters.\",\n      \"status\": \"rendered\",\n      \"path\": \"{output}/figures/cluster_size_barplot.png\",\n      \"skip_reason\": null,\n      \"error\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"plot_id\": \"preprocess_pca_variance\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"backend\": \"python\",\n      \"renderer\": \"pca_variance_curve\",\n      \"filename\": \"pca_variance_curve.png\",\n      \"title\": \"PCA Variance Guidance\",\n      \"description\": \"Explained variance profile used to interpret requested, computed, used, and suggested PC counts.\",\n      \"status\": \"rendered\",\n      \"path\": \"{output}/figures/pca_variance_curve.png\",\n      \"skip_reason\": null,\n      \"error\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"plot_id\": \"preprocess_qc_histograms\",\n      \"role\": \"uncertainty\",\n      \"backend\": \"python\",\n      \"renderer\": \"qc_histograms\",\n      \"filename\": \"qc_metric_distributions.png\",\n      \"title\": \"QC Threshold Context\",\n      \"description\": \"Filtered-data distributions for the main QC metrics with effective threshold overlays.\",\n      \"status\": \"rendered\",\n      \"path\": \"{output}/figures/qc_metric_distributions.png\",\n      \"skip_reason\": null,\n      \"error\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}",
    "report.md": "# Spatial Preprocessing Report\n\n**Date**: 2026-09-30 05:13 UTC\n**Skill**: spatial-preprocess\n**Method**: scanpy_standard\n**Species**: human\n**Data type**: visium\n\n---\n## Summary\n\n- **Method**: scanpy_standard\n- **Raw**: 200 cells x 100 genes\n- **After QC**: 200 cells x 100 genes\n- **HVG selected**: 50\n- **Leiden clusters**: 3\n- **Spatial coordinates**: Yes\n- **Requested PCs**: 15\n- **Computed PCs**: 15\n- **Neighbor graph PCs used**: 15\n- **Suggested PCs**: 16\n- **Primary Leiden resolution**: 0.5\n- **Cluster column**: `leiden`\n- **Spatial key**: `spatial`\n\n### Cluster sizes\n\n| Cluster | Cells |\n|---------|-------|\n| 0 | 75 |\n| 1 | 76 |\n| 2 | 49 |\n\n## Parameters\n\n- `data_type`: visium\n- `species`: human\n- `min_genes`: 5\n- `min_cells`: 0\n- `max_mt_pct`: 20.0\n- `max_genes`: 0\n- `n_top_hvg`: 50\n- `n_pcs`: 15\n- `n_neighbors`: 15\n- `leiden_resolution`: 0.5\n\n### Effective Method Parameters\n\n- `species`: human\n- `tissue_preset`: None\n- `min_genes`: 5\n- `min_cells`: 0\n- `max_mt_pct`: 20.0\n- `max_genes`: 0\n- `n_top_hvg`: 50\n- `n_hvg_selected`: 50\n- `n_pcs_requested`: 15\n- `n_pcs_computed`: 15\n- `n_pcs_used`: 15\n- `n_pcs_suggested`: 16\n- `n_neighbors`: 15\n- `leiden_resolution`: 0.5\n- `normalize_target_sum`: 10000.0\n- `hvg_flavor`: seurat_v3\n- `leiden_flavor`: igraph\n\n## Interpretation Notes\n\n- `processed.h5ad` preserves raw counts in both `adata.layers['counts']` and `adata.raw`, while `adata.X` is the log-normalized matrix used by downstream exploratory workflows.\n- OmicsClaw reports requested, computed, used, and suggested PC counts separately so graph construction choices stay auditable instead of being hidden behind Scanpy internals.\n- The Python gallery is the canonical preprocessing narrative. Optional downstream R styling should consume `figure_data/` instead of recomputing QC, clustering, or embeddings.\n\n## Visualization Outputs\n\n- `figures/manifest.json`: Standard Python gallery manifest\n- `figure_data/`: Figure-ready CSV exports for downstream customization\n- `reproducibility/r_visualization.sh`: Optional R visualization entrypoint\n\n---\n\n## Disclaimer\n\n*OmicsClaw is a research and educational tool for multi-omics analysis. It is not a medical device and does not provide clinical diagnoses. Consult a domain expert before making decisions based on these results.*\n",
